      <div type="clause" n="24.1A">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IudDeiVII">Iud Dei VII</ref> 24.1A</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="Iud Dei VII 24.1A" corresp="#wit-ci"><pb n="414" ed="#liebermann"/>Drihten, soðlice dó þu þis to lofe ⁊ tó wurðunge þinu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þam halegan naman, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ealle menn ongyton ⁊ oncnawon on þe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> þu ert<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IudDeiVII_24-1A.lnote.oe.13"/> ana soð God, þe leofast ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IudDeiVII_24-1A.lnote.oe.16"/> rixast on worulda woruld. Gewyrðe þæt!<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IudDeiVII_24-1A.lnote.oe.17"/></ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 414 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IudDeiVII_24-1A.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">414</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IudDeiVII_24-1A.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">414</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">‘und herrschest in der Ewigkeiten Ewigkeit. Geschehe das!’</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘and reignest for ever and ever. So be it!’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IudDeiVII_24-1A.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">414</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt Iud. Dei II; s. o. S.</hi> 406.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">followed by Iud. Dei II; see above p. 406.</seg></note>
      </div>
